intuition:
OLTP is the cash register. Every transaction is small, fast, and happens constantly. The register needs to be quick and always available. OLAP is the end-of-day report. It runs once, scans everything, and produces a summary. You don't want your end-of-day report locking up the register while customers are in line.

So you run them separately. The register (OLTP) takes orders all day. At night, data gets copied to a separate system (data warehouse) where the OLAP queries run freely without bothering anyone.

